# The image build needs the Go sources, what they embed, the licence files
# and the CA bundle, and nothing else. Listing what goes in, rather than what
# stays out, keeps a checkout's .git, local state, secrets (.env, keys,
# dumps), build output and anything else lying in the directory out of the
# build context and its cache.
*
!go.mod
!go.sum
!cmd/
!internal/
!prompts/
!skills/
!certs/
!LICENSE-*
# Tests and their fixtures are not built into the binary.
**/*_test.go
**/testdata/
